  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n\n\n---\n\n\n**\n¶1:**\n Wisdom,\n which\n the\n Divine\n has\n laid\n open\n from\n its\n conce\nalment\n, was\n disclosed\n to those\n who receive\n instruction\n in\n interior\n things\n. The whole\n full\nness of wisdom\n —\n the Divine\n Truth\n proce\neding from the beginning\n — concerns\n the separation of what\n is good from what is false\n.\n The elevated\n states of the mind were\n raised\n still\n higher, and they\n extended\n themselves\n until\n spiritual\n combat\n should\n arise\n against\n the domin\nion of falsity. In\n the most\n interior\n heights\n, drawn\n from\n every\n state\n of spiritual life, there\n exists\n a pure\n wisdom into\n which nothing\n of\n falsity can enter.\n\n**\n¶2:** Falsity,\n and\n the natural mind in\n which\n it dwells, have\n their origin\n in\n a\n deep\n root\n.\n What poured forth from that\n origin\n is\n what\n the external\n and\n sens\nory\n mind possesses:\n falsity remote\n from all\n wisdom,\n separated\n from it\n by its\n very\n nature.\n\n**¶3:**\n This\n is the first teaching concerning\n the eternal condition\n of these two\n kingdoms\n:\n each\n exists\n in its own right\n, and\n they are divided from one another by their\n essential\n n\natures throughout\n all\n states\n of existence\n. What\n has\n been insc\nribed for you is\n this\n: falsity made\n war against wisdom, desiring to reign\n over an essence not its own. Evil\n seeks dominion over what belongs to good\n. It spread contention through\n the\n spiritual\n order, disturbed every\n state\n of\n peace\n, and rose\n up against\n what\n was above\n it.\n In\n this arose\n the\n great\n crisis\n of the\n soul\n.\n\n**¶4:** The\n Divine\n Power\n came forth — the Divine\n Human in\n its\n first\n and\n in\nmost proce\neding. He took upon\n himself the protective\n truths that\n sur\nround and\n defend\n wisdom\n,\n and\n confront\ned all\n that\n is hostile\n to good\n. He fixed\n evil in restraint by\n those\n very\n truths.\n The\n defending\n tru\nths held\n it\n bound\n.\n\n\n**¶5:** He brought\n forth the Divine\n Love as\n a\n governing\n center\n, and\n all\n the states of wisdom that\n proceed\n from that\n love\n were\n made\n manifest. The Divine\n Proce\neding spread\n out the entire\n spiritual order. He established\n the external\n mind as\n a basis\n.\n Wisdom and falsity,\n which\n from\n the beginning were in\n proximity\n, he\n distinguished\n, and he\n gave external truths as cov\nerings and\n prot\nections. He set in order the progression\n and\n recurring\n cycle of all\n spiritual\n states in their\n elevation\n,\n so that they\n would contin\nually act\n against\n falsity and\n rest\nrain it. He stood firm upon\n what\n is\n imm\novable. He constructed the foundation of\n all\n fundamental truths, and the\n whole order\n was established upon\n them\n.\n\n**¶6:**\n Beneath these\n elevated\n states he\n set\n all\n lower\n things\n in\n order;\n and above\n them\n likewise\n.\n Three\n planes of the natural mind —\n the\n sens\nory,\n the imagin\native, and the rational\n exterior\n — were\n conjoined as\n one\n ground\n. He enclosed the natural mind within four\n elevated states of love toward\n the Divine\n and three containing forms that\n hold\n truth in\n an\n ordered\n way,\n together\n with the\n general knowledges of truth\n and the elevated per\nceptions arranged\n upon\n them. The whole spiritual order stood firm\n as a bond\n and\n restraint upon the\n evil\n powers —\n for\n wisdom had been mingled with falsity\n,\n and the two\n required\n separation\n.\n\n**¶7:** Then\n the Divine\n Medi\nating\n Principle — the third\n proce\neding activity\n of\n the Divine — purified\n wisdom by\n presenting\n its\n own image\n.\n It\n became the means\n of redem\nption for all things:\n that\n which\n draws\n wisdom\n out\n of its\n mixture\n with falsity by\n the\n power of a\n perfect\n form\n.\n\n\n**¶8:** Throughout\n the whole spiritual\n order, self-love blaz\nes and\n cons\numes.\n Yet\n what\n belongs\n to wisdom is also purified by\n that\n very\n process, and ascends to its own\n proper\n essence in\n the Divine\n. Conversely, whatever\n is of\n falsity is drawn\n out\nward and\n gathered into permanent\n restraint. What\n has\n been purified enters into the Divine and\n becomes the very\n perception of celest\nial good.\n All\n re\nde\nemed states\n are\n established\n and\n reign in\n perpetuity, and a single Divine\n comes to be over every\n state\n and\n above\n every state. From\n that\n time forward\n no adversary can\n be\n found against the Father, the\n Sovereign\n of all\n Wisdom —\n the opposition\n has\n ceased\n forever\n.\n\n**¶9:** All\n these states —\n from\n the very\n beginning — exist\n in mixture\n.\n Wisdom and falsity,\n good\n and evil, are inter\ntw\nined and\n joined with one another in\n the\n life\n of every\n soul,\n awa\niting their\n separation\n.\n\n**¶12:** The\n first and\n greatest teaching concerns\n the spiritual\n path\n one\n walks\n through\n the full\nness of all\n states —\n symbol\nized by twelve\n —\n and\n the doc\ntrinal systems and ab\niding\n conditions\n of life found\n within\n the\n mind\n,\n and\n the open\nings of communication\n between interior\n and exterior states that\n are made\n accessible\n within\n them\n,\n and the whole\n natural\n mind\n in\n its complete\n extent\n. And\n my\n struggles\n belong\n to this\n teaching,\n and\n my spiritual\n sufferings —\n for\n what is written\n here\n suff\nices for the person\n who has gained\n wisdom from\n within\n.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "reconstructed_text": "(1) [The] light [of wisdom,] which he has unveiled [from its concealment, (2) he spoke to] his disciples [. (3) The] entire [fullness] of wisdom [, the] word in the beginning [, speaks] concerning the separation [of the light from the darkness.] the heights [were raised] to the heights [,] and they spread out [unt]il they should make war [against the] kingdom [of darkness. The l]ight [that abides] in the heights [, f]rom all the aeons [, is] the light, the one that no [darkness can dwell] in it."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "[This is] the darkness, the world [in which it dwells. From] their root [came that] which poured forth [from the deep,] the one that the earth has [received. It is] darkness [alone, for] it is far from the light [by its very nature.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "This is the first [teaching] concerning the eternality; he [has spoken it] to you, for each one of them exists [in its own nature, and] they are divided from one another by their [essences] in an eternality since the [beginning,] which I have written for you; this is, that [from the first] (4) the darkness has made war against the light, desiring that it would reign over an essence not its own. It spread a quarrel [through every realm;] it disturbed [all that was at peace. It] came up, it [brought all things in this great] need."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "The power came forth from [the Father, that which] is [the Fir]st Man. He [clothed himself in] the armour of light [and opposed] all [the enmity]. He crucified it in [the heights by] the armour [of truth that bound it.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Then] he brought the sun [and the moon forth among] the light aeons [. And the] Living Spirit spread out the universe [and established] the earth [as a foundation. He separated] the light and the darkness in the beginning [, and he fashioned the vessels] and the garments. He gave [them to the luminaries of the heights.] He set in order the [courses of the stars] and the wheel of the course [of all things] in the heights, that they would [purify the light free] of the darkness. He stood firm [and was f]ixed. He constructed the foundation [of the earths, and] all of it was set up."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "Underneath [he set in order] all of them; and also above he [fashioned the thr]e earths, they being conjoined. He enclosed the earth in [the f]our mountains and three vessels [, and placed them] in its seas and its mountains [, and set in] order upon it. This universe stood firm [as] a bond for the evil powers [, for the li]ght that they joined with the darkness [must be separated from it.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "Then the Third Ambassador! [He purified the light] by his image. He became [redeemer of] all things."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "(5) [The powers of darkness,] they are in all the [places of the u]niverse, and the fire blazes in it, and it is devoured [by the fire. Yet] all [the substance] of the light also, and he becomes purifier, and goes up to his essence. Conversely, the darkness which is in [the mixture is drawn] out, and it is gathered in to a bond [. Then shall he] unveil [the purified light,] and they go in to him and become [a sweet pe]rfume [, and are s]et up [an]d they reign for ever, and a single God comes to be [ov]er the totality, being above the totality. You find no opponent from this time on against the Father, the King of the Light and the [aeons of light, for the war shall cease for ever.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "reconstructed_text": "[These are the things] which they occur in, from the beginning [of the world: the light and the darkness,] they are mixed and joined with one another."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 12,
      "reconstructed_text": "(6) The first great lesson [concerns the path] which in the [whole of creation,] that walks in it because of the twelve [constellations that move] in it, which in the cities and the dwelling places found in the [firmament,] because of the doors that are opened in them [and that pour the light down] upon the earth, which in the four corners [of the world. All these things belong to this great teaching, and also my struggles] and my pains. For also [my sorrows] and my afflictions [I have revealed] to them [. This that I have written] suffices for the person [who is a] wise person."
